{title: Clan of Zephon}
{subtitle: Genesis 46:16; 46:26–27; Numbers 26:15; Exodus 6:16; Genesis 47:27}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 71}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Cm7] | [D7] | [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Sons of Gad are named in the [Cm7]list
[D7]Zephon and Haggi hold the [Gm]thread
Shuni and Ezbon join the [Cm7]line
[D7]Eri and Arodi stand the [Gm]test
[Eb]Areli completes the seven [D]names
[Eb]A family bound by blood and [D7]bone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]Seventy souls went down to [Cm7]Egypt
[D7]Jacob’s house escaped the famine’s [Gm]grip
Joseph held power in that [Cm7]land
[D7]But the family kept their ancient [Gm]trust
[Eb]Six-ty-six direct descendants [D]came
[Eb]With wives excluded from the [D]count
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Clan of Zephon in the cen[Cm7]sus
[D7]Counted on the plains of [Gm]Moab
Clan of Zephon in the re[Cm7]cord
[D7]Part of Gad’s enduring [Gm]name
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Israel settled in the land of Gos[Cm7]hen
[D7]Acquired property and [Gm]grew
Fruitful and increased in num[Cm7]ber
[D7]A great nation from the [Gm]seed
[Eb]Zephonite clan within the [D7]tribe
[Eb]A memory kept in the [D7]book
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]From Jacob’s sons to the de[D7]sert
[Eb]The lineage flows like a [D7]river
[Eb]Zephon and Haggi and Shu[D7]ni
[Eb]Their names remain in the scrip[D7]ture
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Seventy persons came to [D7]Egypt
The [Eb]story lives in the [Gm]text
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
